Even chains and scrolls of mail have some use, however marginal.  If nothing
else, they do have weight.  If you can't imagine any use for weight (other
than allowing you to fall down stairs carrying a cockatrice corpse, thus
giving your death a certain dignity from the absurdity of your epitaph) and
don't want to know, DON'T READ ANY FURTHER.

I mean it.

It's the old curse the bag of holding trick.  If you take a bag of holding
that has something in it, and curse it, and then remove and drop that 
something, the bag now has a negative weight proportional to the weight
of what had been in it.  So there have been times when I've been scrounging
around the dungeon looking for some useless piece of junk that had some 
weight.  It's always good for the items to be useless as there's a chance
that they will evaporate when you try to remove them from the cursed bag.

By the way, if you were of the opinion that loadstones are of no use,
I have found them indispensable in getting super high scores.  Suppose
you already have your bag of holding so full that you can only carry it
and one potion of unholy water.  But then you happen to see at your feet 
10,000 uncursed loadstones.  You can pick up loadstones even when you are
collapsing under your load (a nasty feature at most times) so you can 
add their weight to your already hefty bag, and you can produce a bag that
allows you to lift everything you could possibly find or create in the entire
dungeon.

Nothing in the dungeon is totally useless to the hacker with the knowledge
of how to use it.

On the other hand, my nomination for most useless item is a figurine of a 
yellow light.

